<H1><A name=3DSECTION003000000000000000000></A><A =
name=3Dintro></A><BR>1. Python 101=20
-- Introduction to Python </H1>
<P>Python is a high-level general purpose programming language. Because =
code is=20
automatically compiled to byte code and executed, Python is suitable for =
use as=20
a scripting language, Web application implementation language, etc. =
Because=20
Python can be extended in C and C++, Python can provide the speed needed =
for=20
even compute intensive tasks.=20
<P>
<H1><A name=3DSECTION003100000000000000000>1.1 Important Features of =
Python</A>=20
</H1>
<P>
<UL>
  <LI>Built-in high level data types: strings, lists, dictionaries, etc. =

  <P></P>
  <LI>The usual control structures: if, if-else, if-elif-else, while, =
plus a=20
  powerful collection iterator (for).=20
  <P></P>
  <LI>Multiple levels of organizational structure: functions, classes, =
modules,=20
  and packages. These assist in organizing code. An excellent and large =
example=20
  is the Python standard library.=20
  <P></P>
  <LI>Compile on the fly to byte code -- Source code is compiled to byte =
code=20
  without a separate compile step. Source code modules can also be=20
  "pre-compiled" to byte code files.=20
  <P></P>
  <LI>Extensions in C and C++ -- Extension modules and extension types =
can be=20
  written by hand. There are also tools that help with this, for =
example, <B=20
  class=3Dprogram>SWIG</B>, <B class=3Dprogram>sip</B>, <B =
class=3Dprogram>Pyrex</B>.=20
  <P></P></LI></UL>
<P>Some things you will need to know:=20
<P>
<UL>
  <LI>Python uses indentation to show block structure. Indent one level =
to show=20
  the beginning of a block. Out-dent one level to show the end of a =
block. As an=20
  example, the following C-style code:=20
  <P>
  <DIV class=3Dverbatim><PRE>if (x)
{
    if (y)
    {
        f1()
    }
    f2()
}
</PRE></DIV>
  <P>in Python would be:=20
  <P>
  <DIV class=3Dverbatim><PRE>if x:
    if y:
        f1()
    f2()
</PRE></DIV>
  <P>And, the convention is to use four spaces (and no tabs) for each =
level of=20
  indentation.=20
  <P></P></LI></UL>
<P>
